<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1214">1214</a>–1224</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf II was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> who reigned from 1214 to 1224, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-nasir">Muhammad al-Nasir</a> after the catastrophic defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212. He came to the throne young and ruled weakly. The succession crisis following his death produced multiple rival caliphs and defections to Christian kingdoms, accelerating the empire's disintegration.</p></div>
